      ],
      timeline: [
        '1930s-1940s: Manni games diversify across Iceland with regional variations.',
        "1950s: The specific 'Laugavatns' rules for 18 rounds and 6 contracts are established.",
        "1980s: Described in Ãž. GuÃ°mundsson's 'SpilabÃ³k AB' (Icelandic Card Game Book).",
