        'Present: Remains one of the most popular three-player games in Iceland, with a thriving tournament scene.',
      ],
      evolution: "The game's 18-round structure ensures that luck is balanced, as every player must eventually take the difficult 'Nullo' and 'Grand' contracts. The Manni pile exchange adds a strategic element of risk vs. reward.",
      cultural: 'Commonly played during the long Icelandic winter nights; it is considered a game of memory, endurance, and strategic thinking. The HornafjarÃ°armanni variant hosts a World Championship during the summer lobster festival in HornafjÃ¶rÃ°ur.',
