          dealing: "Each player is dealt 16 cards in packets of 4. The remaining 4 cards form the 'Manni' pile, placed face-down in the center.",
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Accumulate the most points by winning tricks relative to your contract target. Game ends after 18 deals (each player plays each of the 6 contracts exactly once).',
          gameplay: "1. **Contract Selection**: Each player must play each of the 6 contracts exactly once over 18 deals. The first time you are declarer, you may choose any contract. The next time, you choose from the remaining 5, and so on. 2. **The Exchange**: Before play begins, the declarer (player to dealer's left) may discard up to 4 cards and draw replacements from the Manni pile. The second player may then exchange up to 4 of the remaining cards. The dealer takes whatever is left in the Manni (if any). 3. **Trick Play**: Declarer leads to the first trick. Must follow suit if possible. If void, may play any card. Highest trump wins, or highest card of led suit if no trumps. Winner leads to next trick.",
          keyRules: [
            'Contracts: Nullo (lose all tricks), Grand (win most tricks), Spades, Hearts, Diamonds, Clubs (suit trumps).',
            'Nullo: No trumps. Ace is low, ranking below the 3.',
            'Grand/Suits: Ace is high.',
            'Grand/Suits target: 8 tricks for declarer, 4 for each defender.',
            'Nullo target: 4 tricks for declarer, 6 for each defender.',
            'Score +1 point for each trick above target, -1 for each trick below target (Nullo is inverted).',
            'Final score = positive points minus negative points.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "Choose your Suit contracts early if you have a strong 6-card suit. Save the Nullo for when you have a hand full of 3s, 4s, and 5s. Never 'waste' a suit contract on a hand without at least one King or Ace. In Nullo, remember the Ace is your friendâ€”it's the lowest card (below the 3).",
          intermediate: "Manni Gambling: If your hand is 'almost' perfect for a Grand (e.g., 10 high cards), exchange your four lowest cards with the Manni. Even if you get worse cards, the risk is often worth it to secure a large point lead. Track which contracts your opponents have leftâ€”they may be forced into unfavorable situations.",
          advanced: "Defensive Teaming: Since it is 3 players, if the declarer chose 'Grand', the other two MUST cooperate to prevent them reaching 8 tricks. Lead suits that your partner is likely void in to force the declarer to use their high cards early. In Nullo, the declarer's target is only 4 tricksâ€”defenders should try to 'force' the declarer to win tricks by leading suits they must follow.",
          tips: [
            "In Nullo, the Ace is the best card because it is 'unbeatable' (it's the lowest). Save your Aces for the end of the round when you might be forced to win.",
            "Keep track of which of the 18 rounds are left. If you still have a 'Nullo' left on round 17, and your hand is high, you are in serious trouble.",
            "Don't be greedy in the Manni exchange. Sometimes keeping a mediocre hand is better than risking a complete disaster.",
            "Watch opponents' discardsâ€”they reveal which suits they are void in.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
